{
  "Scenes.Teladre.ArmorShops.PiercingStudio": "[pg]Right off the bat you see the 'Piercing Studio', its piercing covered centaur sign is a real eye catcher. You can also spot some kind of wolf-man banging away on an anvil in a blacksmith's stand. As well as other shops lining the walls, perhaps those shops will be interesting as well."
  "Scenes.Teladre.ArmorShops.ShoppingDistrict": "The shopping district of Tel'Adre happens to be contained in a large dead end street, with a large set of doors at the entrance to protect it from thieves at night, you'd assume from a higher elevation it would look like a giant square courtyard. Due to the city's shopping area being condensed into one spot, most if not every visible wall has been converted into a store front, in the center of the area are some small stands, guess not everyone can afford a real store."
  "Scenes.Teladre.BarTelAdre.AlteredAppearance": "despite your altered appearance, "
  "Scenes.Teladre.BarTelAdre.CloakedFigure": "[pg]You notice a cloaked figure at the bar, though you're quite unable to discern anything else as its back is turned to you."
  "Scenes.Teladre.BarTelAdre.EdrynHereSitting": "[pg]Edryn, the centauress you met at the gate, is here, sitting down at her table alone and sipping on a glass of wine. You suppose you could go talk to her a bit."
  "Scenes.Teladre.BarTelAdre.EdrynNotPregnant": "[pg]Edryn the centaur isn't pregnant anymore! She waves excitedly at you, beckoning you over to see her. It looks like she's already given birth to your child!"
  "Scenes.Teladre.BarTelAdre.EdrynSippingWine": "[pg]Edryn the centauress is here, sipping wine at a table by herself. She looks up and spots you, her eyes lighting up with happiness. She gives you a wink and asks if you'll join her."
  "Scenes.Teladre.BarTelAdre.EdrynSmilesBeckons": "[pg]Edryn smiles when she sees you and beckons you towards her. Fear and some kind of frantic need are painted across her face, imploring you to come immediately. Whatever the problem is, it doesn't look like it can wait."
  "Scenes.Teladre.BarTelAdre.EdrynUsualPlace": "[pg]Edryn is seated at her usual place, picking at a plate of greens and sipping a mug of the local mead. She looks bored until she sees you. Her expression brightens immediately, and Edryn fiddles with her hair and changes her posture slightly. You aren't sure if she means to, but her cleavage is prominently displayed in an enticing manner."
  "Scenes.Teladre.BarTelAdre.EdrynUsualTable": "[pg]Edryn is seated at her usual table, and chowing down with wild abandon. A stack of plates is piled up next to her. Clearly she has been doing her best to feed her unborn child. She notices you and waves, blushing heavily."
  "Scenes.Teladre.BarTelAdre.EdrynYells": "[pg]Edryn smiles at you and yells, [say: Guess what [name]? I'm pregnant again!] There are some hoots and catcalls but things quickly die down. You wonder if her scent will be as potent as before?"
  "Scenes.Teladre.BarTelAdre.HardlyStares": "you hardly get any odd stares. There are a number of rooms towards the back, as well as a stairway leading up to an upper level."
  "Scenes.Teladre.BarTelAdre.NoBartender": "[pg]It doesn't look like there's a bartender working at the moment."
  "Scenes.Teladre.BarTelAdre.OneNun": "[pg]There is one nun sitting in a corner booth who catches your eye. She sits straight-backed against the dark, wood chair, her thin waist accentuating the supple curve of her breasts. She's dressed in a black robe that looks a few sizes too small for her hips and wears a black and white cloth over her head."
  "Scenes.Teladre.BarTelAdre.RogarHere": "[pg]Ro'gar is here with his back turned to the door, wearing his usual obscuring cloak."
  "Scenes.Teladre.BarTelAdre.ScyllaHabitPoking": "[pg]You see Scylla's white and black nun's habit poking above the heads of the other patrons. The tall woman seems unaware of her effect on those around her, but it's clear by the way people are crowding she's acquired a reputation by now. You're not sure what she's doing, but you could push your way through to find out."
  "Scenes.Teladre.BarTelAdre.ScyllaLeaving": "[pg]It looks like Scylla is here but getting ready to leave. You could check and see what the misguided nun is up to."
  "Scenes.Teladre.BarTelAdre.ScyllaMilling": "[pg]It looks like Scylla is milling around here this morning, praying as she keeps an eye out for someone to 'help'."
  "Scenes.Teladre.BarTelAdre.ScyllaSpotEmpty": "[pg]Scylla's spot in the bar is noticeably empty. She's usually around at this time of day, isn't she? Urta grabs your attention with a whistle and points to a back room with an accompanying wink. Oh... that makes sense. Surely the nun won't mind a little help with her feeding..."
  "Scenes.Teladre.BarTelAdre.UrtaNormallyHere": "[pg]<b>Though Urta would normally be here getting sloshed, her usual spot is completely vacant. You ask around but all you get are shrugs and giggles. Something isn't quite right here. You see an empty bottle of one of her favorite brands of whiskey still rolling on her table, so she can't have been gone long. Maybe she had guard business, or had to head to the back rooms for something?</b>"
  "Scenes.Teladre.BarTelAdre.UrtaPlaceVacant": "[pg]Urta's usual place is vacant, though her table still holds a half-drank mug of something potent and alcoholic. If it's anything like the last time this happened, she's snuck into a back room with Scylla to relieve some pressure. It might not hurt to join in..."
  "Scenes.Teladre.BarTelAdre.WetBitchInterior": "The interior of The Wet Bitch is far different than the mental picture its name implied. It looks like a normal tavern, complete with a large central hearth, numerous tables and chairs, and a polished dark wood bar. The patrons all seem to be dressed and interacting like normal people, that is if normal people were mostly centaurs and dog-{0} of various sub-species. The atmosphere is warm and friendly, and "
  "Scenes.Teladre.BuyCarrotFromOswald.AcquiredCarrot": "[pg](<b>Acquired Key Item: Carrot</b>)"
  "Scenes.Teladre.BuyCarrotFromOswald.GemsChangeHands": "Gems change hands in a flash, and you're now the proud owner of a bright orange carrot!"
  "Scenes.Teladre.DiscoverTelAdre.DesertSands": "The merciless desert sands grind uncomfortably under your [feet] as you walk the dunes, searching the trackless sands to uncover their mysteries. All of a sudden, you can see the outline of a small city in the distance, ringed in sandstone walls. Strangely it wasn't there a few moments before. It's probably just a mirage brought on by the heat. Then again, you don't have any specific direction you're heading, what could it hurt to go that way?"
  "Scenes.Teladre.DiscoverTelAdre.InvestigateCity": "[pg]Do you investigate the city in the distance?"
  "Scenes.Teladre.DiscoverTelAdre.ProwlingDunes": "While out prowling the desert dunes you manage to spy the desert city of Tel'Adre again. You could hike over to it again, but some part of you fears being rejected for being 'impure' once again. Do you try?"
  "Scenes.Teladre.EncounterTelAdre.AsksHorseWoman": "[say: What's the problem, {0}? A demon make it through the barrier?] asks the imposing horse-woman.[pg]{1} head, replying, [say: I don't think so, Edryn. {2} something else. We should use the crystal and see if [he]'s fit to be allowed entry to Tel'Adre.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.EncounterTelAdre.BarksHoldIt": "[say: Hold it!] barks the {0} bristling in suspicion at your sudden appearance, [say: What's your business in the city of Tel'Adre?][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.EncounterTelAdre.DetectingThoughts": "As if detecting your thoughts, {0} drops the bottle and pulls out a halberd much longer than {1} is tall.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.EncounterTelAdre.FindGuarding": "Once again you find the {0} guarding the gates. {1} companion, Edryn, once again. The centauress advances cautiously, and you submit herself to her inspection as she once again produces her magical amulet. "
  "Scenes.Teladre.EncounterTelAdre.NothingToLose": "Deciding you've nothing to lose by complying, you stand there, awaiting whatever reinforcements this {0} has summoned. Within the minute, a relatively large-chested centauress emerges from a smaller door cut into the gate, holding a massive bow with an arrow already nocked.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.EncounterTelAdre.PlacesHand": "She places one hand on your shoulder and holds the crystal in the other. Her eyes close, but her brow knits as she focuses on something. "
  "Scenes.Teladre.EncounterTelAdre.ShrugsExplains": "You shrug and explain that you know nothing about this town, and just found it while exploring the desert. The {0} stares at you skeptically for a moment and then blows a shrill whistle. {1} orders, [say: No sudden moves.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.EncounterTelAdre.SlogsSands": "You slog through the shifting sands for a long time, not really seeming to get that close. Just when you're about to give up, you crest a large dune and come upon the walls of the city you saw before. It's definitely NOT a mirage. There are sandstone walls at least fifty feet tall ringing the entire settlement, and the only entrance you can see is a huge gate with thick wooden doors. The entrance appears to be guarded by a {0} who's more busy sipping on something from a bottle than watching the desert.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.EncounterTelAdre.WatchesCentaur": "You watch the big centaur cautiously as she pulls out a pendant, and approaches you. [say: Hold still,] she says, [say: this will do you no harm.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.Houses.RaphaelOffer": "[pg]You remember Raphael's offer about the Orphanage, but you might want to see about shaping yourself more to his tastes first. He is a picky fox, after all, and you doubt he would take well to seeing you in your current state."
  "Scenes.Teladre.Houses.WhoseHome": "Whose home will you visit?"
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCream.AsksGentle": "[pg][say:Hey there. Are you lost?] it asks, gentle and low. You turn around. A man stands there, his silhouette tall and broad against the bright, red-tinged sky behind him. [say:Are you here with your mom or dad? Do they know where you are?]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCream.CrouchedEntrance": "[pg]He spends another few moments crouched in the entrance of the alley, which is barely wide enough to accommodate him, a contemplative hand on his chin. [say:You know,] he finally says, [say:you look like you could really use some ice cream. It's great for places like this, cheer you right up! Would you like that? Would you like some ice cream?]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCream.HearsVoice": "[pg]It's then that you hear a voice behind you."
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCream.HotDustyRoads": "The hot, dusty roads of Tel'Adre haven't been treating you well as you attempt to pass through. It only takes an errant gust of wind to send you into a coughing fit, and it's feeling more and more like the sun beating down on your head is doing so quite literally. You're getting woozy enough that you need some cover, and quick."
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCream.LooksExpectantly": "[pg]He looks at you expectantly with his bright blue eyes. Do you want a treat?"
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCream.NearbyAlley": "[pg]A nearby alley looks suitable for your needs. It's far enough from the road itself that you're able to slip clear of the crowd, and when you finally duck into the cool shadows, you let out a deep breath, feeling like you've just gotten out from under a stifling blanket. You're not entirely sure how you're going to deal with the heat when you have to leave this shelter."
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCream.NodContinues": "[pg][say:You mean you're all alone?] You nod, and he continues, [say:Here in the middle of the desert? That's terrible!] He pauses for a second and looks off at an indistinct point to the side. [say:Just terrible... You look pretty out of it. The desert around here's definitely no joke, you need to be careful.]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCream.ShakesHeadNo": "[pg]You shake your head no, and he crouches down, giving you a better view of his appearance. He's middle-aged, but still fit, clothed in a bulky leather traveling cloak with a large number of pouches and straps. A flat cap sits on top of his short shock of dark brown hair, and he wears a smile on his clean-shaven face."
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCreamNo.AsksSmilesWarmly": "[pg][say:Are you sure?] he asks. [say:When I first got here, it looked like you were about to pass out. You need something to freshen you up, let me treat you.] He smiles warmly at you."
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCreamNo.NotReallySure": "You're not really sure about this. You tell the strange man that you don't want anything from him, and there are a few moments of silence. All you can hear is his quiet breathing in the desert air, and the faint murmur of the crowds that now seem far away. A small shiver runs through you."
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCreamNoFinal.LeftDisconcerted": "[pg]You're left with a somewhat disconcerted feeling. You watch the man's back as he fades into the crowd and wonder exactly what he was doing there. You find no answer by the time you can't see him any more, but you linger a few moments longer in the shade, recovering and trying to regain the strength to face the blazing sun once more."
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCreamNoFinal.NothingLeft": "[pg]And then, with nothing left to do, you move on."
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCreamNoFinal.ShakesHeadFirmly": "You shake your head firmly. You feel another chill in the resulting silence, even with the blazing heat of the city. The man's shoulders roll forward, and your heart thumps once, but he only stretches to his feet and grunts."
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCreamNoFinal.TakeCareYourself": "[pg][say:Well, try to take care of yourself. It's really important, especially for a growing [boy] like yourself. Please, talk to a guard or an adult you trust if you ever need help,] he says. The man then tips his cap, giving you a brief flash of some sort of animal ears, and smiles one last time, just as warmly as the rest, before turning about and striding off into the city."
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCreamRun.DontKnowWhat": "You don't know exactly what's going on, but you know you shouldn't be here. The heat might have been suffocating, but if you spend one more moment trapped in this cramped alleyway, you're not sure what's going to happen. The only question is how exactly you'll do it. He's big, but it doesn't look like he's very ready to react, so you might have an opportunity."
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCreamRun.FeelsSafety": "[pg]It's only when you feel a modicum of safety that you're willing to turn back to look. You're breathing hard, and you're fully ready to set off again in a second should you need to, but strangely, you don't. The man hasn't moved at all, hasn't even shifted from his lazy crouch. He cranes his neck over and peers in your direction, a vaguely disappointed expression on his face."
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCreamRun.NothingMoreToDo": "[pg]Whatever the case, there's nothing more to do but to continue on under the desert sun."
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCreamRun.RiskIt": "[pg]You'll just have to risk it. In the middle of a sentence you haven't been listening to, you suddenly dash forward, skirting the gap between his leg and the wall. It's a tight fit, but you make it, and your [legs] continue working for a bit afterwards, doing their best to bear you a safe distance away."
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCreamRun.SenseUnease": "[pg]Your sense of unease isn't really dying down, but he breaks the spell by rising to his feet and stretching languidly. As you stay there trapped between bolting and observing him a bit longer, he suddenly breaks off at a brisk pace, not even paying you a passing glance as he presses on through the crowd. It's only seconds before you can't see him any longer, and you're left feeling unsure of whether you read the situation right."
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCreamYes.ArrivesHolding": "[pg][say:Hey there,] he says as he arrives, holding up a small white swirl of heavenly ambrosia. [say:Hope you like vanilla.]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCreamYes.GivesAffirmation": "[pg][say:Feeling better, right?] You give him your affirmation, and he chuckles softly. [say:Wonderful. It's great that you're alright, but please remember to take care of yourself. The sun can be a real meanie sometimes, so you should make sure to drink a lot and watch out for the heat.]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCreamYes.GlanceUp": "[pg]You glance up to see the stranger's gaze focused in a hazy direction to the right. You wait a few moments, but his steady hands stay still on your [skinshort], and he doesn't say anything further, so you continue eating your ice cream. It's not one bit less delicious, though it is starting to melt a bit, your pace quickening in response."
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCreamYes.HeadInclines": "[pg][say:Go on, don't let me stop you.] His head inclines towards the cone in your grasp. You suppose that that's the most pressing concern right now, so you get back to it, eagerly tasting that sugary bliss once again. It's enough that you have to close your eyes, and you feel incredibly grateful that you're sitting here safe and serene in this alley, instead of out there in the heat. You're so content that you aren't very startled when the man's hands slip forward onto your [if (tailLeg) {tail|thighs}], stroking you lightly."
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCreamYes.LickAfterLick": "[pg]Lick after lick, the frosty treat shrinks until only the cone remains. A few crunches, and that's gone too, leaving you with just a faint chill in your hands and mouth. Your benefactor sees that you've finished, and with the warm smile you've come to expect from him, releases your [if (singleleg) {body|legs}] after one final squeeze."
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCreamYes.NotTooPicky": "[pg]You're not too picky at the moment, so you happily take the cone from his offering hand and bring it to your lips. When the first taste of ice cream hits your tongue, you almost melt, a palpable sense of relief washing over you. You rock in place as the sweet sensation interferes with your balance."
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCreamYes.ParticularlyPleased": "[pg]He seems particularly pleased for some reason, but only a few seconds pass before he eases you onto your [feet] and rises. A quick nod signals his farewell, and he's off, striding into the street crowd with a brisk step. It's only seconds before you can't make his shape out any more."
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCreamYes.PutsForth": "[pg][say:Woah there, you look a bit unsteady,] the man puts forth. [say:Here, let me help.] Before you can react, he takes your arm and tugs you over a few steps before sitting on an abandoned crate and patting his lap. You're not quite sure, but his guiding hand leads you over, and you settle down on top of him. His body is broad and firm, making for a reasonably comfortable seat."
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCreamYes.SaysGrinning": "[say:Great,] he says, grinning even wider than before, [say:that's just great! You stay here for a minute, I'll go get you a treat.] A single wink, and he's off, his long legs carrying him out of sight surprisingly quickly."
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCreamYes.StrangeEncounter": "[pg]A strange encounter, to be sure, but you're feeling quite refreshed and ready to take on the desert city once more."
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCreamYes.TastesGood": "[pg][say:Hmm, tastes good, right? I've been in this city a long time, and it's still a comfort every time...]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.IceCreamYes.WaitsUncertain": "[pg]You wait uncertain for a few minutes as the crowds continue to shift and stir in front of you. You're not really sure of his trustworthiness, but the prospect of something cold and soothing to drive off the oppressive heat is all you can think of. Almost anything would be better than suffering in the stinging air outside your shelter, so you're even quite glad when you see the man's large frame resolve out of the mass of pedestrians once more."
  "Scenes.Teladre.OswaldBuyMenu.AsksAnything": "You ask if Oswald has anything to sell. He nods and says, [say: Certainly. If you don't see anything that interests you, come back tomorrow. We get new stocks of merchandise all the time.]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.OswaldBuyMenu.FirstItemLine": "\n{0}: {1}"
  "Scenes.Teladre.OswaldBuyMenu.PricesBanner": "[pg]<b><u>Oswald's Prices</u></b>"
  "Scenes.Teladre.OswaldBuyMenu.SecondItemLine": "\n{0}: {1}"
  "Scenes.Teladre.OswaldBuyMenu.ThirdItemLine": "\n{0}: {1}"
  "Scenes.Teladre.OswaldPawn.CanSellItem": "(You can sell an item here, but Oswald will not let you buy them back, so be sure of your sales.)"
  "Scenes.Teladre.OswaldPawn.CantAfford": "[pg]<b>You can't afford that!</b>"
  "Scenes.Teladre.OswaldPawn.CloserInspection": "Upon closer inspection, you realize the pawnbroker{0}. He doesn't look entirely comfortable and he slouches, but he manages to smile the entire time. His appearance is otherwise immaculate, including his classy suit-jacket and tie, though he doesn't appear to be wearing any pants. Surprisingly, his man-bits are retracted. "
  "Scenes.Teladre.OswaldPawn.FiddlingTopHat": "You see Oswald fiddling with a top hat as you approach his stand again. He looks up and smiles, {0} hands together. He asks, [say: Have any merchandise for me {1}?][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.OswaldPawn.IntroducesOswald": "The dog{0} introduces himself as Oswald and gives his pitch, [say: Do you have anything you'd be interested in selling? The name's Oswald, and I'm the best trader in Tel'Adre.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.OswaldPawn.MentionCarrot": "[pg]In passing, you mention that you're looking for a carrot."
  "Scenes.Teladre.OswaldPawn.StandMess": " His stand is a disheveled mess, in stark contrast to its well-groomed owner. He doesn't appear to be selling anything at all right now.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.OswaldPawn.TopHatTips": "[pg]Oswald's top hat tips precariously as his ears perk up, and he gladly announces, [say: I happen to have come across one recently - something of a rarity in these dark times, you see. I could let it go for 500 gems, if you're interested.]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.OswaldPawn.WhatAShame": "What a shame, but maybe you can give him a reason to stand up straight?"
  "Scenes.Teladre.OswaldPawn.WhoWouldThought": "Who would've thought that seeing someone NOT aroused would ever shock you?"
  "Scenes.Teladre.OswaldPawnMenu.CanSellItem": "(You can sell an item here, but Oswald will not let you buy them back, so be sure of your sales. You can shift-click to sell all items in a selected stack.)"
  "Scenes.Teladre.OswaldPawnMenu.EstimatesBanner": "[pg]<b><u>Oswald's Estimates</u></b>"
  "Scenes.Teladre.OswaldPawnMenu.FiddlingTopHat": "You see Oswald fiddling with a top hat as you approach his stand again. He looks up and smiles, {0} hands together. He asks, [say: Have any merchandise for me {1}?][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.OswaldPawnMenu.GemsFor": "\n{0} gems for {1}."
  "Scenes.Teladre.OswaldPawnSell.HandsOverItem": "You hand over {0} to Oswald. He shrugs and says, [say: Well ok, it isn't worth anything, but I'll take it.]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.OswaldPawnSell.HandsOverItemAgain": "You hand over {0} to Oswald. He nervously pulls out {1} gems and drops them into your waiting hand."
  "Scenes.Teladre.OswaldPawnSell.HandsOverQuantity": "You hand over {0} {1} to Oswald. He shrugs and says, [say: Well ok, it isn't worth anything, but I'll take it.]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.OswaldPawnSell.HandsOverQuantityAgain": "You hand over {0} {1} to Oswald. He nervously pulls out {2} gems and drops them into your waiting hand."
  "Scenes.Teladre.OswaldPawnSellAll.LaysOutItems": "You lay out all the items you're carrying on the counter in front of Oswald. He examines them all and nods. Nervously, he pulls out {0} gems and drops them into your waiting hand."
  "Scenes.Teladre.OswaldTransactBuy.AfterExamining": "After examining what you've picked out with his fingers, Oswald hands it over, names the price and accepts your gems with a curt nod.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.OswaldTransactBuy.ConsiderPurchase": "You consider making a purchase, but you lack the gems to go through with it."
  "Scenes.Teladre.RanisPaysBounty.GivesNod": "He gives you a nod and waves you off as you head into Tel'Adre."
  "Scenes.Teladre.RanisPaysBounty.RanisStopsGate": "As you enter the city, Ranis stops you at the gate. [say: I heard about your help with catching that nuisance of a fox. He's never been particularly dangerous, but he's certainly made himself a constant pain in the ass, and stolen enough valuables from gullible women to build up quite the bounty.] He lifts a leather sack from the ground beside him, the telltale clinking of gems sounding from it as he passes it over to you. [say: One thousand gems. Your assistance is appreciated, I'm sure those useless wolves wouldn't have been able to catch him on their own.]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreCrystal.BeforeAnswer": "Before you can answer, the centaur steps in, standing between {0} and yourself. [say: {1}, can you take my post, please? I'll show [him] around the city. I'll work an extra shift later, if you need me to.][pg]{2} frowns, questioning her for a moment, but then shrugs and accepts, moving towards the gate."
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreCrystal.EdrynBreathes": "[pg]After the {0} leaves, Edryn breathes deeply and stares at you. You briefly recoil at the rather imposing sight, but she smiles and extends a hand towards you, blushing slightly. [say: Come on, kid. You've been through hell walking through that desert. Take my hand.]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreCrystal.GesturesDoor": "The {0} gestures towards the smaller door and asks, [say: Would you like a tour of Tel'Adre, newcomer?][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreCrystal.HandsMotionless": "[pg]Your hands stand motionless on the air for a few moments, looking for something to grab. Finding no other option, you put them on her toned abdomen. She tenses up for a moment when you first grab hold, but she soon relaxes and begins moving towards the city."
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreCrystal.PendantShimmers": "The crystal pendant shimmers, vibrating in place and glowing a purple hue. Edryn steps back, watching you warily, [say: You've been deeply touched by corruption. You balance on a razor's edge between falling completely and returning to sanity. You may enter, but we will watch you closely.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreCrystal.PendantTwirls": "The crystal pendant twirls in place, glowing a dull red. Edryn takes a small step back and murmurs, [say: You've seen the darkness of this land first hand, but its hold on you is not deep. You'll find sanctuary here. The demons cannot find this place yet, and we promise you safe passage within the walls.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreCrystal.PendantVibrates": "The crystal pendant begins to vibrate in the air, swirling around and glowing dangerously black. Edryn snatches her hand back and says, [say: I'm sorry, but you're too far gone to step foot into our city. If by some miracle you can shake the corruption within you, return to us.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreCrystal.RemembersEtiquette": "You remember your etiquette and nod, thankful to have a quick introduction to such a new place. {0} leaves Edryn to watch the gate and leads you inside.{1}. The door closes behind you easily as you step into the city of Tel'Adre..."
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreCrystal.ShinesWhite": "The crystal shines a pale white light. Edryn steps back and smiles broadly at you and says, [say: You've yet to be ruined by the demonic taint that suffuses the land of Mareth. Come, you may enter our city walls and find safety here, though only so long as the covenant's white magic protects us from the demons' lapdogs.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreCrystal.ShrugsStepsBack": "You shrug and step back. You could probably defeat these two, but you know you'd have no hope against however many friends they had beyond the walls. You turn around and leave, a bit disgruntled at their hospitality. After walking partway down the dune you spare a glance over your shoulder and discover the city has vanished! Surprised, you dash back up the dune, flinging sand everywhere, but when you crest the apex, the city is gone."
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreCrystal.ThinksAboutIt": "[pg]You think about it for a moment, but decide to go ahead and hold her hand. With a groan and a swift motion, she lifts you from the ground and swings you to her back. You almost lose your balance and fall, but you manage to sit on her. [say: Comfortable back there? I'll show you around the town. Hang onto something, but don't pull on my hair, or you'll regret it.]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreMenu.MassiveCity": "Tel'Adre is a massive city, though most of its inhabitants tend to hang around the front few city blocks. It seems the fall of Mareth did not leave the city of Tel'Adre totally unscathed. A massive tower rises up in the center of the city, shimmering oddly. From what you overhear in the streets, the covenant's magic-users slave away in that tower, working to keep the city veiled from outside dangers. There does not seem to be a way to get into the unused portions of the city, but you'll keep your eyes open.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreMenu.SignCentaur": "A sign depicting a hermaphroditic centaur covered in piercings hangs in front of one of the sandstone buildings, and bright pink lettering declares it to be the 'Piercing Studio'. You glance over and see the wooden facade of {0}ou can also spot some kind of wolf-man banging away on an anvil in a blacksmith's stand, and a foppishly-dressed dog-man with large floppy ears seems to be running some kind of pawnshop in his stand. Steam boils from the top of a dome-shaped structure near the far end of the street, and simple lettering painted on the dome proclaims it to be a bakery. Perhaps those shops will be interesting as well."
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreTour.BeforeAnswer": "Before you can answer, {0}"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreTour.BlushWord": "blush"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreTour.ChuckleWord": "chuckle"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreTour.FindsCenter": "The two of you find yourselves in the center of a busy intersection. {0} explains that this is the main square of the city, and that, although the city is large, a goodly portion of it remains empty. Much of the population left to assist other settlements in resisting the demons and was lost. {1} brushes a lock of stray hair from {2} eye and guides you down the road, making sure to point out {3} favorite pub - \"The Wet Bitch\". You "
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreTour.FurtherOnPiercing": "A bit further on, you're shown a piercing parlor, apparently another favorite of {0}. A cute human girl with cat-like ears peeks out the front and gives you both a friendly wave. It's so strange to see so many people together in one place, doing things OTHER than fucking. The whole thing makes you miss your hometown more than ever. Tears come to your eyes unbidden, and you wipe them away, glad to at least have this one reminder of normalcy. {1} politely pretends not to notice{2} wraps up the tour.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreTour.LeadsStreets": "{0} leads you into the streets of Tel'Adre, giving you a brief run-down of {1} city, [say: You see, about two decades back, the demons were chewing their way through every settlement and civilization in Mareth. The covenant, a group of powerful magic-users, realized direct confrontation was doomed to fail. They hid us in the desert with their magic, and the demons can't corrupt what they can't find. So we're safe, for now.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreTour.OnShoulderSays": "{0} on the shoulder and says, [say: Okay, gotta go! Be good and stay out of trouble, alright?][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreTour.SuggestiveName": " at the rather suggestive name as {0} turns around and says, [say: With how things are, we've all gotten a lot more comfortable with our sexuality. I hope it doesn't bother you.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreTourLoli.AfterFewMinutes": "[pg]After moving forwards for a few minutes, the two of you find yourselves in the center of a busy intersection. Many citizens stare and gawk at the kid riding on top of one of the city guards, making you and Edryn both blush, but she continues moving anyway. Edryn explains that this is the main square of the city, and that, although the city is large, a goodly portion of it remains empty. [say: I don't want to make you afraid, but see all those empty houses? Those were other people that tried to fight the demons. They didn't come back, [name]. Please, think about what you're doing.] She raises a hand to call your attention and points to a certain store. A bakery!"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreTourLoli.BeforeAnswer": "Before you can answer, she's taken off, back to the city gates. Well, you're free to do whatever you want now."
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreTourLoli.BriefRunDown": "[pg]She gives you a brief run down on the city. [say: About twenty years ago, some really bad demons were doing really bad things to people in Mareth. The covenant, a group of powerful and kind wizards, wanted to protect good folks like you and me from the demons. They hid us in the desert with their magic, and in here, we're all safe. You don't have to worry about demons here, understand?] She turns her head to attempt to face you, asking you for a response. You nod. She smiles, and faces forward again.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreTourLoli.CentauressShows": "[pg]Another centauress shows up from behind the counter. [say: Oh, hey Edryn! I didn't know your shift was over. And who's this kid?] Edryn moves in and introduces you to her. [say: This is [name], [he] showed up outside the walls a few minutes ago. Can you give [him] something to replenish [his] energies? A cookie or a cupcake. I'll pay for it later.]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreTourLoli.CouldPay": " You could probably pay for it yourself, but refusing a gift, even something as simple as a cookie, might be considered rude."
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreTourLoli.EntersStore": "[pg]Edryn enters the store and pulls you from her back. The smell inside the bakery is great, the scent of fresh bread and sweets awakens the glutton inside you, and you immediately feel hungry."
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreTourLoli.EyesDrawnSign": "[pg]Your eyes are drawn to a particular sign in the main square, \"The Wet Bitch\". You poke at the centauress' shoulder and ask what that is. She groans before answering. [say: That's a popular pub. You'll probably find me and {0} there quite often, though you probably shouldn't enter, because-, since I-... Just don't drink anything that isn't water! It's not for kids.] You're slightly offended by the belittling, but you don't make much of it."
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreTourLoli.EyesWidening": "[say: <b>WHAT?</b> What kind of sick bastard picks an innocent child as--] She notices your eyes widening in surprise. [say: I-I mean... that's... very brave of you. But look, you know you can just stay here, right? Leave those quests to the adults.] You explain Ingnam is important to you, and, although you're scared, you have a duty to fulfill. She sighs, faces forward, and continues moving."
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreTourLoli.FurtherOnPiercing": "[pg]A bit further on, you're shown a piercing parlor. A cute human girl with cat-like ears peeks out the front and gives you both a friendly wave. It's so strange to see so many people together in one place, doing things OTHER than fucking. The whole thing makes you miss your hometown more than ever. Tears come to your eyes unbidden, and you wipe them away, glad to at least have this one reminder of normalcy. Edryn scratches her head when she notices, unsure of how to handle this situation. [say: Don't worry, [name]. Home is where you make it, and this is a pretty good place to call home!] Her enthusiasm trails off into a sigh when she notices her motivational speak didn't really work."
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreTourLoli.GallopsStreets": "Edryn gallops down into the streets of Tel'Adre. [say: What's your name, little {0}?] she asks, while greeting some passerby. You remember your etiquette and answer with respect. [say: I'm [name], miss.] Edryn laughs. [say: Miss? Hah, what a polite young [boy] you are.]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreTourLoli.LeaveBakery": "[pg]The two of you leave the bakery soon after. She extends her hand again, and you mount her, continuing your tour."
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreTourLoli.MovesTowardsCenter": "Edryn continues to move towards the center of the city. [say: With that story in mind, [name], just where did you come from, and how did you find this city?] You puff up and explain your status as the chosen Champion of Ingnam and your quest to protect your village from any threat. Edryn stops moving and, again, bends her head to try to face you.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreTourLoli.NotLikeYou": " Well, it's not like you'd be able to pay for it. You're pretty broke."
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreTourLoli.TakesChocolateChip": "[pg][say: Sure, Edryn, sure! Here you go.] She takes a big chocolate chip cookie and hands it to you. It's pretty much fresh out of the oven, warm and crumbly, with the chocolate drops almost melting on your hands. You devour it in an instant, bringing a smile to Edryn's face. This might just be the tastiest thing you've had ever since you left Ingnam."
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreTourLoli.WalksBackSquare": "[pg]She walks back to the main square, stops and helps you dismount her. [say: I gotta go protect the city, ok, [name]? Stay out of trouble, and if someone asks for... s-e-x, I, uh, just- stay out of trouble, alright?][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.UrtaIsABadass.CommotionStreets": "There's a commotion in the streets of Tel'Adre. A dense crowd of onlookers has formed around the center of the street, massed together so tightly that you're unable to see much, aside from the backs the other onlookers' heads. The sound of blows impacting on flesh can be heard over the crowd's murmuring, alerting you of the fight at the gathering's core."
  "Scenes.Teladre.WatchUrtaBeABadass.ArousedWord": "aroused"
  "Scenes.Teladre.WatchUrtaBeABadass.BarksGetThis": "{0} barks, [say: Get this one outside the walls before he wakes. I won't have this corrupted filth in our city, and make sure you get the wards updated. If he manages to find his way back, you sorry excuses for guards will be going out with him.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.WatchUrtaBeABadass.ByWhatSee": " by what you see. A pair of thick, demonic horns curve back over the beast's head, piercing through the bottoms of its wolf-like ears. Its entire body is covered in rippling muscle, leaving you in no doubt of its strength. Even with a broken knee, the wolf-man is clearly aroused: protruding from a bloated sheath, his massive dog-dick is fully erect, solid black in color, with an engorged knot. Small white worms crawl over the surface of his penis, wriggling out of the tip and crawling down the length, leaving trails of slime behind them.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.WatchUrtaBeABadass.CanidCharges": "The bigger canid charges, snarling, with his claws extended. {0} sidesteps and pivots, {1} momentum carrying {2} foot around in a vicious kick. {3} foot hits the side of the beast's knee hard enough to buckle it, and the wolf goes down on his knees with an anguished cry. {4} slips under his arm and twists, turning his slump into a fall. A cloud of dust rises from the heavy thud of the beast's body as it slams into the cobblestone street.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.WatchUrtaBeABadass.ConfusedWord": "confused"
  "Scenes.Teladre.WatchUrtaBeABadass.FewDogsArmor": "A few dog-{0} in similar armor to {1} approach and lash ropes around the wolf's legs. They hand a line to a centaur, and together the party begins dragging the unconscious body away. With the action over, the crowd begins dispersing. More than a few {2} leaves."
  "Scenes.Teladre.WatchUrtaBeABadass.HorrifiedWord": "horrified"
  "Scenes.Teladre.WatchUrtaBeABadass.KneelsDown": "{0} kneels down onto the corrupted wolf's throat, cutting off its air as it foams and struggles under {1}. With grim determination, {2} holds the weakening, demonically-tainted wolf underneath {3}, leaning all of {4} body-weight into {5} knee to keep it down. It struggles for what seems like ages, but eventually the tainted wolf's eyes roll closed. {6} nods and rises, watching closely as the beast's breathing resumes.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.WatchUrtaBeABadass.NowImmobile": "Now that it's immobile, you get can get a better look at the defeated combatant, and you're "
  "Scenes.Teladre.WatchUrtaBeABadass.ShoulderPast": "You shoulder past the bulky centaurs, ignore the {0} of the nearby wolves and hounds as {1} against you, and press your way through to the center of the crowd. Eventually the throng parts, revealing the embattled combatants. A snarling wolf, nearly eight feet tall, towers over {2}. The {3} is girded in light leather armor and dripping with sweat. The larger wolf-man is staggering about, and his {4} with blood.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.Weaponshop.Desc": "For all types of pain-dealing tools."
  "Scenes.Teladre.Weaponshop.Title": "Weaponsmith"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreMenu.Pawn": "Pawn"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreMenu.OswaldBuy": "Buy"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreMenu.OswaldSell": "Sell"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreMenu.OswaldBuyCarrot": "Buy Carrot"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreMenu.OswaldKathAlley": "Kath's Alley"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TelAdreMenu.OswaldSafehouse": "Safehouse"
  "Scenes.Teladre.UrtaBadass.Commotion": "There's a commotion in the streets of Tel'Adre. A dense crowd of onlookers has formed around the center of the street, massed together so tightly that you're unable to see much, aside from the backs the other onlookers' heads. The sound of blows impacting on flesh can be heard over the crowd's murmuring, alerting you of the fight at the gathering's core."
  "Scenes.Teladre.UrtaBadass.PressThrough": "You shoulder past the bulky centaurs, ignore the {0} of the nearby wolves and hounds as {1} against you, and press your way through to the center of the crowd. Eventually the throng parts, revealing the embattled combatants. A snarling wolf, nearly eight feet tall, towers over {2}. The {3} is girded in light leather armor and dripping with sweat. The larger wolf-man is staggering about, and his {4} with blood.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.UrtaBadass.Fight": "The bigger canid charges, snarling, with his claws extended. {0} sidesteps and pivots, {1} momentum carrying {2} foot around in a vicious kick. {3} foot hits the side of the beast's knee hard enough to buckle it, and the wolf goes down on his knees with an anguished cry. {4} slips under his arm and twists, turning his slump into a fall. A cloud of dust rises from the heavy thud of the beast's body as it slams into the cobblestone street.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.UrtaBadass.Beast": "Now that it's immobile, you can get a better look at the defeated combatant, and you're {0} by what you see. A pair of thick, demonic horns curve back over the beast's head, piercing through the bottoms of its wolf-like ears. Its entire body is covered in rippling muscle, leaving you in no doubt of its strength. Even with a broken knee, the wolf-man is clearly aroused: protruding from a bloated sheath, his massive dog-dick is fully erect, solid black in color, with an engorged knot. Small white worms crawl over the surface of his penis, wriggling out of the tip and crawling down the length, leaving trails of slime behind them.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.UrtaBadass.Kneel": "{0} kneels down onto the corrupted wolf's throat, cutting off its air as it foams and struggles under {1}. With grim determination, {2} holds the weakening, demonically-tainted wolf underneath {3}, leaning all of {4} body-weight into {5} knee to keep it down. It struggles for what seems like ages, but eventually the tainted wolf's eyes roll closed. {6} nods and rises, watching closely as the beast's breathing resumes.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.UrtaBadass.Barks": "{0} barks, [say: Get this one outside the walls before he wakes. I won't have this corrupted filth in our city, and make sure you get the wards updated. If he manages to find his way back, you sorry excuses for guards will be going out with him.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.UrtaBadass.DragAway": "A few dog-{0} in similar armor to {1} approach and lash ropes around the wolf's legs. They hand a line to a centaur, and together the party begins dragging the unconscious body away. With the action over, the crowd begins dispersing. More than a few {2} leaves."
  "Scenes.Teladre.DiscoverTelAdre.1": "The merciless desert sands grind uncomfortably under your [feet] as you walk the dunes, searching the trackless sands to uncover their mysteries. All of a sudden, you can see the outline of a small city in the distance, ringed in sandstone walls. Strangely it wasn't there a few moments before. It's probably just a mirage brought on by the heat. Then again, you don't have any specific direction you're heading, what could it hurt to go that way?"
  "Scenes.Teladre.DiscoverTelAdre.2": "[pg]Do you investigate the city in the distance?"
  "Scenes.Teladre.DiscoverTelAdre.3": "While out prowling the desert dunes you manage to spy the desert city of Tel'Adre again. You could hike over to it again, but some part of you fears being rejected for being 'impure' once again. Do you try?"
  "Scenes.Teladre.EncounterTelAdre.1": "You slog through the shifting sands for a long time, not really seeming to get that close. Just when you're about to give up, you crest a large dune and come upon the walls of the city you saw before. It's definitely NOT a mirage. There are sandstone walls at least fifty feet tall ringing the entire settlement, and the only entrance you can see is a huge gate with thick wooden doors. The entrance appears to be guarded by a {0} who's more busy sipping on something from a bottle than watching the desert.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.EncounterTelAdre.2": "As if detecting your thoughts, {0} drops the bottle and pulls out a halberd much longer than {1} is tall.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.EncounterTelAdre.3": "[say: Hold it!] barks the {0} bristling in suspicion at your sudden appearance, [say: What's your business in the city of Tel'Adre?][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.EncounterTelAdre.4": "You shrug and explain that you know nothing about this town, and just found it while exploring the desert. The {0} stares at you skeptically for a moment and then blows a shrill whistle. {1} orders, [say: No sudden moves.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.EncounterTelAdre.5": "Deciding you've nothing to lose by complying, you stand there, awaiting whatever reinforcements this {0} has summoned. Within the minute, a relatively large-chested centauress emerges from a smaller door cut into the gate, holding a massive bow with an arrow already nocked.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.EncounterTelAdre.6": "[say: What's the problem, {0}? A demon make it through the barrier?] asks the imposing horse-woman.[pg]{1} head, replying, [say: I don't think so, Edryn. {2} something else. We should use the crystal and see if [he]'s fit to be allowed entry to Tel'Adre.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.EncounterTelAdre.7": "You watch the big centaur cautiously as she pulls out a pendant, and approaches you. [say: Hold still,] she says, [say: this will do you no harm.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.EncounterTelAdre.8": "She places one hand on your shoulder and holds the crystal in the other. Her eyes close, but her brow knits as she focuses on something. "
  "Scenes.Teladre.EncounterTelAdre.9": "Once again you find the {0} guarding the gates. {1} nods at you and whistles for {2} companion, Edryn, once again. The centauress advances cautiously, and you submit herself to her inspection as she once again produces her magical amulet. "
  "Scenes.Teladre.Crystal.1": "The crystal pendant begins to vibrate in the air, swirling around and glowing dangerously black. Edryn snatches her hand back and says, [say: I'm sorry, but you're too far gone to step foot into our city. If by some miracle you can shake the corruption within you, return to us.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.Crystal.2": "You shrug and step back. You could probably defeat these two, but you know you'd have no hope against however many friends they had beyond the walls. You turn around and leave, a bit disgruntled at their hospitality. After walking partway down the dune you spare a glance over your shoulder and discover the city has vanished! Surprised, you dash back up the dune, flinging sand everywhere, but when you crest the apex, the city is gone."
  "Scenes.Teladre.Crystal.3": "The crystal pendant shimmers, vibrating in place and glowing a purple hue. Edryn steps back, watching you warily, [say: You've been deeply touched by corruption. You balance on a razor's edge between falling completely and returning to sanity. You may enter, but we will watch you closely.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.Crystal.4": "The crystal pendant twirls in place, glowing a dull red. Edryn takes a small step back and murmurs, [say: You've seen the darkness of this land first hand, but its hold on you is not deep. You'll find sanctuary here. The demons cannot find this place yet, and we promise you safe passage within the walls.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.Crystal.5": "The crystal shines a pale white light. Edryn steps back and smiles broadly at you and says, [say: You've yet to be ruined by the demonic taint that suffuses the land of Mareth. Come, you may enter our city walls and find safety here, though only so long as the covenant's white magic protects us from the demons' lapdogs.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.Crystal.6": "The {0} gestures towards the smaller door and asks, [say: Would you like a tour of Tel'Adre, newcomer?][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.Crystal.7": "Before you can answer, the centaur steps in, standing between {0} and yourself. [say: {1}, can you take my post, please? I'll show [him] around the city. I'll work an extra shift later, if you need me to.][pg]{2} frowns, questioning her for a moment, but then shrugs and accepts, moving towards the gate."
  "Scenes.Teladre.Crystal.8": "[pg]After the {0} leaves, Edryn breathes deeply and stares at you. You briefly recoil at the rather imposing sight, but she smiles and extends a hand towards you, blushing slightly. [say: Come on, kid. You've been through hell walking through that desert. Take my hand.]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.Crystal.9": "[pg]You think about it for a moment, but decide to go ahead and hold her hand. With a groan and a swift motion, she lifts you from the ground and swings you to her back. You almost lose your balance and fall, but you manage to sit on her. [say: Comfortable back there? I'll show you around the town. Hang onto something, but don't pull on my hair, or you'll regret it.]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.Crystal.10": "[pg]Your hands stand motionless on the air for a few moments, looking for something to grab. Finding no other option, you put them on her toned abdomen. She tenses up for a moment when you first grab hold, but she soon relaxes and begins moving towards the city."
  "Scenes.Teladre.Crystal.11": "You remember your etiquette and nod, thankful to have a quick introduction to such a new place. {0} leaves Edryn to watch the gate and leads you inside.{1}. The door closes behind you easily as you step into the city of Tel'Adre..."
  "Scenes.Teladre.TourLoli.1": "Edryn gallops down into the streets of Tel'Adre. [say: What's your name, little {0}?] she asks, while greeting some passerby. You remember your etiquette and answer with respect. [say: I'm [name], miss.] Edryn laughs. [say: Miss? Hah, what a polite young [boy] you are.]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TourLoli.2": "[pg]She gives you a brief run down on the city. [say: About twenty years ago, some really bad demons were doing really bad things to people in Mareth. The covenant, a group of powerful and kind wizards, wanted to protect good folks like you and me from the demons. They hid us in the desert with their magic, and in here, we're all safe. You don't have to worry about demons here, understand?] She turns her head to attempt to face you, asking you for a response. You nod. She smiles, and faces forward again.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TourLoli.3": "Edryn continues to move towards the center of the city. [say: With that story in mind, [name], just where did you come from, and how did you find this city?] You puff up and explain your status as the chosen Champion of Ingnam and your quest to protect your village from any threat. Edryn stops moving and, again, bends her head to try to face you.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TourLoli.4": "[say: <b>WHAT?</b> What kind of sick bastard picks an innocent child as--] She notices your eyes widening in surprise. [say: I-I mean... that's... very brave of you. But look, you know you can just stay here, right? Leave those quests to the adults.] You explain Ingnam is important to you, and, although you're scared, you have a duty to fulfill. She sighs, faces forward, and continues moving."
  "Scenes.Teladre.TourLoli.5": "[pg]After moving forwards for a few minutes, the two of you find yourselves in the center of a busy intersection. Many citizens stare and gawk at the kid riding on top of one of the city guards, making you and Edryn both blush, but she continues moving anyway. Edryn explains that this is the main square of the city, and that, although the city is large, a goodly portion of it remains empty. [say: I don't want to make you afraid, but see all those empty houses? Those were other people that tried to fight the demons. They didn't come back, [name]. Please, think about what you're doing.] She raises a hand to call your attention and points to a certain store. A bakery!"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TourLoli.6": "[pg]Edryn enters the store and pulls you from her back. The smell inside the bakery is great, the scent of fresh bread and sweets awakens the glutton inside you, and you immediately feel hungry."
  "Scenes.Teladre.TourLoli.7": "[pg]Another centauress shows up from behind the counter. [say: Oh, hey Edryn! I didn't know your shift was over. And who's this kid?] Edryn moves in and introduces you to her. [say: This is [name], [he] showed up outside the walls a few minutes ago. Can you give [him] something to replenish [his] energies? A cookie or a cupcake. I'll pay for it later.]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TourLoli.8": " Well, it's not like you'd be able to pay for it. You're pretty broke."
  "Scenes.Teladre.TourLoli.9": " You could probably pay for it yourself, but refusing a gift, even something as simple as a cookie, might be considered rude."
  "Scenes.Teladre.TourLoli.10": "[pg][say: Sure, Edryn, sure! Here you go.] She takes a big chocolate chip cookie and hands it to you. It's pretty much fresh out of the oven, warm and crumbly, with the chocolate drops almost melting on your hands. You devour it in an instant, bringing a smile to Edryn's face. This might just be the tastiest thing you've had ever since you left Ingnam."
  "Scenes.Teladre.TourLoli.11": "[pg]The two of you leave the bakery soon after. She extends her hand again, and you mount her, continuing your tour."
  "Scenes.Teladre.TourLoli.12": "[pg]Your eyes are drawn to a particular sign in the main square, \"The Wet Bitch\". You poke at the centauress' shoulder and ask what that is. She groans before answering. [say: That's a popular pub. You'll probably find me and {0} there quite often, though you probably shouldn't enter, because-, since I-... Just don't drink anything that isn't water! It's not for kids.] You're slightly offended by the belittling, but you don't make much of it."
  "Scenes.Teladre.TourLoli.13": "[pg]A bit further on, you're shown a piercing parlor. A cute human girl with cat-like ears peeks out the front and gives you both a friendly wave. It's so strange to see so many people together in one place, doing things OTHER than fucking. The whole thing makes you miss your hometown more than ever. Tears come to your eyes unbidden, and you wipe them away, glad to at least have this one reminder of normalcy. Edryn scratches her head when she notices, unsure of how to handle this situation. [say: Don't worry, [name]. Home is where you make it, and this is a pretty good place to call home!] Her enthusiasm trails off into a sigh when she notices her motivational speak didn't really work."
  "Scenes.Teladre.TourLoli.14": "[pg]She walks back to the main square, stops and helps you dismount her. [say: I gotta go protect the city, ok, [name]? Stay out of trouble, and if someone asks for... s-e-x, I, uh, just- stay out of trouble, alright?][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.TourLoli.15": "Before you can answer, she's taken off, back to the city gates. Well, you're free to do whatever you want now."
  "Scenes.Teladre.Tour.1": "{0} leads you into the streets of Tel'Adre, giving you a brief run-down of {1} city, [say: You see, about two decades back, the demons were chewing their way through every settlement and civilization in Mareth. The covenant, a group of powerful magic-users, realized direct confrontation was doomed to fail. They hid us in the desert with their magic, and the demons can't corrupt what they can't find. So we're safe, for now.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.Tour.2": "The two of you find yourselves in the center of a busy intersection. {0} explains that this is the main square of the city, and that, although the city is large, a goodly portion of it remains empty. Much of the population left to assist other settlements in resisting the demons and was lost. {1} brushes a lock of stray hair from {2} eye and guides you down the road, making sure to point out {3} favorite pub - \"The Wet Bitch\". You "
  "Scenes.Teladre.Tour.3": "blush"
  "Scenes.Teladre.Tour.4": "chuckle"
  "Scenes.Teladre.Tour.5": " at the rather suggestive name as {0} turns around and says, [say: With how things are, we've all gotten a lot more comfortable with our sexuality. I hope it doesn't bother you.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.Tour.6": "A bit further on, you're shown a piercing parlor, apparently another favorite of {0}. A cute human girl with cat-like ears peeks out the front and gives you both a friendly wave. It's so strange to see so many people together in one place, doing things OTHER than fucking. The whole thing makes you miss your hometown more than ever. Tears come to your eyes unbidden, and you wipe them away, glad to at least have this one reminder of normalcy. {1} politely pretends not to notice{2} wraps up the tour.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.Tour.7": "{0} on the shoulder and says, [say: Okay, gotta go! Be good and stay out of trouble, alright?][pg]"
  "Scenes.Teladre.Tour.8": "Before you can answer, {0}"
  "Scenes.Teladre.Houses.UrtasHouse": "Urta's House"
  "Scenes.Teladre.Houses.Arians": "Arian's"
  "Scenes.Teladre.Houses.Orphanage": "Orphanage"
  "Scenes.Teladre.Shops.Street": "The shopping district of Tel'Adre happens to be contained in a large dead end street, with a large set of doors at the entrance to protect it from thieves at night, you'd assume from a higher elevation it would look like a giant square courtyard. Due to the city's shopping area being condensed into one spot, most if not every visible wall has been converted into a store front, in the center of the area are some small stands, guess not everyone can afford a real store."
  "Scenes.Teladre.Shops.Second": "[pg]Right off the bat you see the 'Piercing Studio', its piercing covered centaur sign is a real eye catcher. You can also spot some kind of wolf-man banging away on an anvil in a blacksmith's stand. As well as other shops lining the walls, perhaps those shops will be interesting as well."
}
